---@class polymarket.data.GetActivityRequest
---@field user? string Required; the feed is user-anchored.
---@field limit? number Page size; default 100, max 1000, past-cap rejected.
---@field cursor? string Opaque cursor from a prior response's `next_cursor`; binds the sort direction it was minted under.
---@field type? string Activity type(s), comma-separated. Accepted values: `TRADE`, `SPLIT`, `MERGE`, `REDEEM` (automatic redemptions included), `CONVERSION`, `MIGRATION`, `REWARD`, `YIELD`, `MAKER_REBATE`, `TAKER_REBATE`, `REFERRAL_REWARD`, `DEPOSIT`, `WITHDRAWAL`, `DIRECTIONAL_SPLIT`, `DIRECTIONAL_MERGE`, `THRESHOLD_COMPOSE`, `THRESHOLD_DECOMPOSE`, `TIP`. Any other value is rejected with `400`. Omitted, the feed returns every type except `TIP`. `DEPOSIT` and `WITHDRAWAL` rows are returned only with `exclude_deposits_withdrawals=false`. Under its default (`true`) they are dropped even when named here, so `type=DEPOSIT` or `type=WITHDRAWAL` alone returns an empty page. `DIRECTIONAL_SPLIT`, `DIRECTIONAL_MERGE`, `THRESHOLD_COMPOSE` and `THRESHOLD_DECOMPOSE` are operations on range events, whose outcomes are value buckets and whose lines are ABOVE / BELOW positions over those buckets. A directional split turns collateral plus the buckets between two lines into ABOVE the lower line and BELOW the higher one; a directional merge reverses it. Both are rows of the whole event, so a `condition` filter never returns them. A threshold compose turns buckets into one line position and a threshold decompose turns it back; these rows carry the line's market and side. Split, merge, redeem and conversion on a range event keep `SPLIT`, `MERGE`, `REDEEM` and `CONVERSION`. `TIP` is **opt-in**: it is never in the default set, so it is only returned when you name it here. A tip is a user↔user pUSD transfer that is not a trade-settlement leg; `size` is the amount and `side` carries the direction (`IN` received / `OUT` sent).
---@field condition? string Condition id(s), comma-separated (at most 20 distinct values). `condition_id` / `conditionId` are accepted aliases.
---@field event_id? string Gamma event id(s), comma-separated (at most 20 distinct values); resolves to the events' markets. Mutually exclusive with `condition`.
---@field side? string BUY or SELL.
---@field start? number Window start on `block_timestamp`, epoch seconds (inclusive). Omitted or `0` floors to three years back; pass `start=1` for full history.
---@field ["end"]? number Window end, epoch seconds (inclusive); omitted or `0` means now plus one day.
---@field sort_by? string Only `TIMESTAMP` is supported (v2 pages by keyset).
---@field sort_direction? string `ASC` or `DESC` (default). The keyset seeks in the chosen direction; the minted cursor binds it, so pass it consistently when paging.
---@field exclude_deposits_withdrawals? boolean Defaults to `true`, which drops `DEPOSIT` and `WITHDRAWAL` rows from the page, including when `type` names them. Pass `false` to include them.

---@class polymarket.data.GetApprovalsRequest
---@field user? string The proxy wallet whose approval state to return. Required EVM address.

---@class polymarket.data.GetBiggestWinnersRequest
